            <ArticleTitle>Retropsoas hernia as a cause of chronic abdominal pain: CT diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>312-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Congenital retropsoas small bowel herniation is reported as the cause of long-standing recurrent abdominal pain in a teenage girl. Knowledge of this entity is important for differential diagnosis of abdominal pain, mass, or retroperitoneal gas and fluid, and for avoiding complications of percutaneous renal interventions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
